WEBVTT

00:02:56.916 --> 00:03:00.956
Our Rutland ichthyosaur lived
during the early Jurassic,

00:03:00.996 --> 00:03:04.716
around about 180 million years ago.

00:03:06.796 --> 00:03:10.156
This is a time when Rutland
was deep underwater,

00:03:10.196 --> 00:03:12.836
covered by an ancient tropical sea.

00:03:13.436 --> 00:03:17.956
Now I spent most of my professional career

00:03:17.996 --> 00:03:19.796
of around 14 years

00:03:19.836 --> 00:03:23.076
studying thousands of ichthyosaurs.

00:03:24.276 --> 00:03:27.196
And this has been a great pleasure
to travel around the world,

00:03:27.236 --> 00:03:29.156
study lots and lots of ichthyosaurs.

00:03:29.156 --> 00:03:31.636
And so when I received these photos,